# coin_combinations_unordered:
# CSES 1636, Coin Combinations II (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1636), in our
# own words: given coin values, each positive, each usable any number of times,
# the number of ways to produce the sum target when the order of the coins does not
# matter (two ways are the same when they use each coin of the list equally
# often), modulo 10^9 + 7. The input is a Scott list of binary naturals (the
# coins, taken as distinct positions of the list) and a binary natural target. Part of
# the CSES port's second batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: a way is the sequence of its coins in
# the order of the list, so the list of all ways is built from the running sum
# partial_sum = 0 upwards over a suffix of the coin list (no way once partial_sum > target, the empty way
# once partial_sum = target, otherwise each coin of the suffix put in front of the ways of
# partial_sum + coin over the suffix that starts at coin), and its length is counted in binary and
# reduced modulo 10^9 + 7. Its reading is exponential in target even under tabling,
# since the ways themselves are built and counted; the replacement the family
# asks for is the knapsack recurrence over the coins in turn, ways(partial_sum) += ways(partial_sum -
# coin) for each coin with the sums ascending, on fixed-width integers modulo
# 10^9 + 7.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only: its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal (the sum
# 10^9 + 7 and the numerals are written with binary_zero, binary_even and
# binary_odd). It β-reduces to V, the canonical binary numeral of the answer:
# every recursion ends, since ways consumes the bounded gap target - partial_sum (every coin is
# positive, so partial_sum grows by at least one and the recursion stops once partial_sum exceeds target),
# its inner loop a finite suffix, and every other recursion consumes a finite
# list or a binary numeral. So the β reduction reaches V; the branches that a
# Scott boolean discards are never read. ../common/binary_modular's
# binary_modulo, which writes no top, is called with the positive modulus only.
# So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable equations for the
# contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero binary_even binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ _ _ binary_modulo
. (λtuple. tuple λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd binary_zero)
λ modulus
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λself count items. items count λ_ tail. self (merge_binary_increment count) tail
  )
λ count_from
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ coins target
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self suffix partial_sum
        . binary_less_than target partial_sum nil
        λ. merge_binary_equality partial_sum target (cons nil nil)
        λ. fixpoint
          ( λ along rest
            . rest nil λcoin later. append (map (cons coin) λ. self rest λ. merge_binary_plus partial_sum coin) λ. along later
          ) suffix
      ) coins binary_zero
  )
λ sequences
. (λtuple. tuple λcoins target. binary_modulo (count_from binary_zero λ. sequences coins target) modulus)
λ coin_combinations_unordered
. export coin_combinations_unordered
